  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$-18-303=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The answer will be negative since $-18$ is negative, and we're subtracting $303$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n18+303\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the addition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{ }1\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n18+303=321.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-18-303=-321.\n$$",
